# Data. all_data.csv alone is 16.4 GB and git never forgets a blob, so this
# has to be right before the first commit rather than after.
data/*
# ...except the category vocabulary. It is 800 bytes, app.py reads it at
# import, and a deployment that ships the model without it cannot start.
!data/categories.json
# ...and a 2,000-customer sample, so a visitor to the deployed page has
# something to upload without a 16 GB download first.
!data/demo_data.parquet
!data/demo_labels.parquet

# Trained artifacts. Rebuild them locally with `python code/pipeline.py train`.
models/*
# ...except the one run that is deployed, which has to travel with the code:
# 6.4 MB, and a serving container with no model in it is just a crash. Ship a
# different model by changing this line and the pin in app.py together, so
# swapping what production scores with is a visible edit rather than a side
# effect of retraining.
!models/latest.json
!models/20260921-205141-s42/

# Scoring output
predictions.parquet

